  "operative_text": "Sec. 51 (amending G.L. c. 140, new s. 128B(a)): Section 128B. (a) No person shall possess, own, offer for sale, sell or otherwise transfer in the commonwealth or import into the commonwealth an assault-style firearm, or a large capacity feeding device.\nSec. 39 (amending G.L. c. 140 s. 122(b)): (b) No person shall knowingly possess, manufacture, assemble, offer for sale, sell or otherwise transfer or import an untraceable firearm in the commonwealth;\nSec. 39 (amending G.L. c. 140 s. 122(a)(1)): Section 122. (a)(1) The department of criminal justice information services shall develop and maintain a real time electronic firearms registration system.\nSec. 45 (amending G.L. c. 140, new s. 124C(a)): Section 124C. (a) A person with a temporary license issued under section 124B shall not purchase, rent or lease a firearm or ammunition in the commonwealth without a valid permit to purchase issued under this section.\nSec. 58 (amending G.L. c. 140, new s. 131(a)): Section 131. (a) A petitioner who believes that a person holding a license or permit under section 124 to 124B, inclusive, may pose a risk of causing bodily injury to self or others may, on a form furnished by the court and signed under the pains and penalties of perjury, file a petition in court.\nSec. 63 (adding G.L. c. 258E s. 4A): Section 4A. Upon issuance of a temporary or emergency order under section 5 or 6, the court shall, if the plaintiff demonstrates a substantial likelihood of immediate danger of harassment, order the immediate suspension and surrender of any firearms license or permit that the defendant may hold and order the defendant to surrender all firearms and ammunition that the defendant then controls, owns or possesses in accordance with this chapter,\nSec. 127: A valid license to carry a firearm issued under sections 131 or 131F of chapter 140 of the General Laws, a valid firearm identification card under section 129B of said chapter 140 or a valid license to sell under section 122 of said chapter 140, shall remain valid until the expiration of said license and shall entitle the holder to possess the firearms authorized by the license at the time it was last issued or renewed;"
}